@*
    ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    BnSwitch — Phase 7.3 Task 1.2 (design decision 1 + 2), authored in
    .razor.

    Emits the `switch` element → NodeType 9. Android: SwitchMaterial/Switch.
    iOS: UISwitch — the SAME widget BnCheckbox maps to there (design
    decision 2: iOS has no native checkbox, so the two controls are
    semantically identical on iOS and visually distinct only on Android; the
    recorded "renders natively, not identically" divergence lives in
    BnCheckbox's header and is not restated here).

    The wire, the events, the enabled semantics, the bind-loop guard, the
    fixed-intrinsic-size measurement and the loud-garbage posture are
    BnCheckbox's, verbatim — one prose home (BnCheckbox.razor), two NodeTypes.
    The only difference IS the NodeType: 8 vs 9 is what lets each shell pick
    its widget class at CreateNode (decision 1 — the class must be chosen
    before any prop arrives).
    ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*@
@inherits BnLayoutItem
<switch value="@(Checked ? "true" : "false")"
        enabled="@(Enabled ? null : "false")"
        @attributes="ItemAttributes"
        @onchange="HandleChange" />

@code {
    /// <summary>Whether the switch is on.</summary>
    [Parameter] public bool Checked { get; set; }

    /// <summary>Raised with the new state when the user toggles it — the
    /// write-back half of the <c>@bind-Checked</c> pair.</summary>
    [Parameter] public EventCallback<bool> CheckedChanged { get; set; }

    /// <summary>Set false to show the platform's disabled control and stop it
    /// responding. Default true.</summary>
    [Parameter] public bool Enabled { get; set; } = true;

    private Task HandleChange(ChangeEventArgs e)
        => CheckedChanged.InvokeAsync(
            BnCheckbox.ParseBoolPayload(e.Value?.ToString(), "switch"));
}
